Hi Linda,

Third arm this month with two servos on ID 1. All new STS3215s ship with ID 1 and the same baud rate, so if one gets mounted without being set, the bus scan finds a conflict and nothing works until we take the arm apart.

Proposal: set IDs on the bench before anything gets mounted. One servo at a time on the driver board, run the motor setup script, put a small numbered dot sticker (1-6) on the case. Takes about 2 minutes per arm.

Can we add it as step 1 of servo prep?

Avery

-- 
Avery Brooks
Robotics Engineer | Northwind Robotics
avery.brooks@northwind.example

