Hi both,

Two customer arms came back this month with "Overload" errors on shoulder_lift (motor 2). Both were 7.4 V arms running off the 3 A supply that ships with the hobby kit.

On the bench: with the arm at full reach and a 300 g load, shoulder_lift pulls well over 2 A for a moment when it starts moving. With the 3 A brick the voltage sags and the servo trips its protection. With a 5 A supply I can't make it happen.

Suggestion: ship every kit with a 5 A supply. It's about $2 more per kit.

Avery

-- 
Avery Brooks
Robotics Engineer | Northwind Robotics
avery.brooks@northwind.example

